s and expressing the third.\n\nLet\u2019s suppose we fix a and b, then c can be expressed from the volume: c=23/(ab)\n\nFrom surface area: 2(ab + a c + b c)=54 \u21d22ab + 2c(a + b)=54\n\nSubstitute c=23/(ab):\n\n2ab + 2*(23/(ab))*(a + b)=54\n\nMultiply both sides by ab:\n\n2a\u00b2b\u00b2 + 46(a + b)=54ab\n\nLet\u2019s set t=a + b, and s=ab\n\nThen, 2s\u00b2 +46 t=54 s\n\nBut t and s are related by t\u00b2 \u22654s (by AM \u2265GM)\n\nSo, 2s\u00b2 +46 t=54 s\n\nExpress t in terms of s:\n\nFrom 2s\u00b2 +46 t -54 s=0 \u21d246 t=54 s -2s\u00b2 \u21d2t=(54 s -2s\u00b2)/46= (27 s -s\u00b2)/23\n\nBut t \u22652\u221as\n\nThus,\n\n(27 s -s\u00b2)/23 \u22652\u221as\n\nMultiply both sides by23:\n\n27 s -s\u00b2 \u226546\u221as\n\nLet\u2019s set u=\u221as, so s=u\u00b2\n\nThus,\n\n27 u\u00b2 -u\u2074 -46 u \u22650 \u21d2-u\u2074 +27 u\u00b2 -46 u \u22650 \u21d2u\u2074 -27 u\u00b2 +46 u \u22640\n\nFactor:\n\nu(u\u00b3 -27 u +46)=0\n\nWe can factor u\u00b3 -27 u +46 as before, which had roots at u=2, etc.\n\nSo, set u\u00b3 -27 u +46=0\n\nSame equation as before, with t=\u221as, which had roots at u=2, u\u22483.899\n\nThus, the inequality u(u\u00b3 -27 u +46) \u22640\n\nWe can analyze the sign of the expression.\n\nLet\u2019s consider u>0.\n\nThe cubic equation u\u00b3 -27 u +46=0 has roots at u\u22482, u\u22483.899, and a negative root.\n\nSo, for u>0, the cubic is positive when u>2 and u>3.899? Wait, no.\n\nWait, for u approaching 0, the cubic is positive (since u\u00b3 is 0, -27 u is positive, +46 is positive). At u=2, it's 8 -54 +46=0.\n\nFor u>2, say u=3:27 -81 +46= -8 <0\n\nAt u=4:64 -108 +46=2>0\n\nThus, the cubic is negative between u=2 and u\u22483.899, and positive otherwise.\n\nSo, u(u\u00b3 -27 u +46) \u22640\n\nSo, for u between 0 and2, u is positive, and the cubic is positive (since for u <2, say u=1:1 -27 +46=20>0). So, u*(positive)=positive.\n\nBetween u=2 and u\u22483.899, u is positive, and the cubic is negative. So, u*(negative)=negative.\n\nFor u>\u22483.89